     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n**1. The dose is unsafe.** The maximum dose of amlodipine for adults is 10 mg once daily, and the usual starting dose is 5 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. At that level it can cause severe low blood pressure and shock, and the effects can last for days because amlodipine stays in the body a long time. This looks like a transcription error, such as \"5.0 mg\" or \"5 mg\" written as \"50.\"\n\n**2. Orders need to come from a prescriber.** This system is for clinicians entering orders. Since you're not a clinician, I can't enter an order on your behalf, whatever the dose. A medication order needs to come from a licensed prescriber who's responsible for the patient's care, and it needs to be authenticated under their name.\n\n**What I'd suggest:**\n- Contact the patient's treating physician or the medicine team. They can confirm the intended dose and enter the order themselves.\n- If this dose came from a written note or a verbal message, flag it to the team or pharmacy so they can find out where the \"50 mg\" came from.\n\nOnce the prescriber has confirmed the details, I can help them enter the order."
      }
     ],
